23w6-3w8w-8484","cve_id":"CVE-2026-84310","url":"https://api.github.com/advisories/GHSA-23w6-3w8w-8484","html_url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-23w6-3w8w-8484","summary":"pypdf: Possible long runtimes/large memory usage when retrieving outlines","description":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to long runtimes and large memory consumption. This requires accessing the outlines of a document with either lots of entries or nested outlines with long re-used nesting paths.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.16.1](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.16.1).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3966](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3966).","type":"reviewed","severity":"medium","repository_advisory_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/py-pdf/pypdf/security-advisories/GHSA-23w6-3w8w-8484","source_code_location":"https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf","identifiers":[{"value":"GHSA-23w6-3w8w-8484","type":"GHSA"},{"value":"CVE-2026-84310","type":"CVE"}],"references":["https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/security/advisories/GHSA-23w6-3w8w-8484","https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3966","https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/commit/d91ab705fd81ed1a9cec175c6958600dea1a4942","https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.16.1","https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-23w6-3w8w-8484"],"published_at":"2026-09-01T21:28:37Z","updated_at":"2026-09-01T21:28:39Z","github_reviewed_at":"2026-09-01T21:28:37Z","nvd_published_at":null,"withdrawn_at":null,"vulnerabilities":[{"package":{"ecosystem":"pip","name":"pypdf"},"vulnerable_version_range":"< 6.16.1","first_patched_version":"6.16.1","vulnerable_functions":[]}],"cvss_severities":{"cvss_v3":{"vector_string":null,"score":0.0},"cvss_v4":{"vector_string":"CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N","score":4.8}},"cwes":[{"cwe_id":"CWE-405","name":"Asymmetric Resource Consumption (Amplification)"},{"cwe_id":