om/users/stefan6419846/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefan6419846/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefan6419846/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefan6419846/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"type":"analyst"}],"cvss":{"vector_string":null,"score":null},"epss":{"percentage":0.00166,"percentile":0.05144}},{"ghsa_id":"GHSA-wjqc-6w8f-h24c","cve_id":"CVE-2026-48735","url":"https://api.github.com/advisories/GHSA-wjqc-6w8f-h24c","html_url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-wjqc-6w8f-h24c","summary":"pypdf: Manipulated XMP metadata streams can exhaust RAM","description":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to large memory usage. This requires parsing large XMP metadata, possibly with lots of unnecessary elements.\n\n### Patches\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.12.1](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.12.1).\n\n### Workarounds\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3796](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3796).","type":"reviewed","severity":"medium","repository_advisory_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/py-pdf/pypdf/security-advisories/GHSA-wjqc-6w8f-h24c","source_code_location":"https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf","identifiers":[{"value":"GHSA-wjqc-6w8f-h24c","type":"GHSA"},{"value":"CVE-2026-48735","type":"CVE"}],"references":["https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/security/advisories/GHSA-wjqc-6w8f-h24c","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-48735","https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3796","https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.12.1","https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-wjqc-6w8f-h24c"],"published_at":"2026-06-16T13:45:58Z","updated_at":"2026-06-16T13:45:59Z","github_reviewed_at":"2026-06-16T13:45:58Z","nvd_published_at":"2026-05-28T16:16:29Z","withdrawn_at":null,"vulnerabilities":[{"package":{"ecosystem":"pip","name":"pypdf"},"vulnerable_version_range":"< 