,"repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kodareef5/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kodareef5/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kodareef5/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"type":"reporter"},{"user":{"login":"stefan6419846","id":96178532,"node_id":"U_kgDOBbuRZA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96178532?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefan6419846","html_url":"https://github.com/stefan6419846","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefan6419846/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefan6419846/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefan6419846/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefan6419846/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefan6419846/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefan6419846/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefan6419846/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefan6419846/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefan6419846/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"type":"analyst"}],"cvss":{"vector_string":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:L","score":5.3},"epss":{"percentage":0.00515,"percentile":0.41533}},{"ghsa_id":"GHSA-87mj-5ggw-8qc3","cve_id":"CVE-2026-33699","url":"https://api.github.com/advisories/GHSA-87mj-5ggw-8qc3","html_url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-87mj-5ggw-8qc3","summary":"pypdf: Possible infinite loop during recovery attempts in DictionaryObject.read_from_stream","description":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to an infinite loop. This requires reading a file in non-strict mode.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.9.2](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.9.2).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf users cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3693](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3693).","type":"reviewed","severity":"medium","repository_advisory_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/py-pdf/pypdf/security-advisories/GHSA-87mj-5ggw-8qc3","source_code_location":"https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf","identifiers":[{"value":"GHSA-87mj-5ggw-8qc3","type":"GHSA"},{"value":"CVE-2026-33699","type":"CVE"}],"references":["https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/security/advisories/GHSA-87mj-5ggw-8qc3","https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3693","https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.9.2","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-33699","https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-87mj-5ggw-8qc3"],"published_at":"2026-03-25T20:05:22Z","updated_at":"2026-03-27T21:36:44Z","github_reviewed_at":"2026-03-25T20:05:22Z","nvd_published_at":"2026-03-27T01:16:19Z","withdrawn_at":null,"vulnerabilities":[{"package":{"ecosystem":"pip","name":"pypdf"},"vulnerable_version_range":"< 6.9.2","first_patched_version":"6.9.2","vulnerable_functions":[]}],"cvss_severities":{"cvss_v3":{"vector_string":null,"score":0.0},"cvss_v4":{"vector_string":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N/E:U","score":4.6}},"cwes":[{"cwe_id":"CWE-835","name":"Loop with Unreachable Exit Condition ('Infinite Loop')"}],"credits":[{"user":{"login":"kejcao","id":106453563,"node_id":"U_kgDOBlhaOw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106453563?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kejcao","html_url":"https://github.com/kejcao","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kejcao/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kejcao/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kejcao/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kejcao/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kejcao/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kejcao/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kejcao/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kejcao/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kejcao/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"type":"reporter"},{"user":{"login":"stefan6419846","id":96178532,"node_id":"U_kgDOBbuRZA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96178532?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefan6419846","html_url":"https://github.com/stefan6419846","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefan6419846/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefan6419846/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefan6419846/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefan6419846/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefan6419846/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefan6419846/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefan6419846/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefan6419846/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefan6419846/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"type":"analyst"}],"cvss":{"vector_string":null,"score":null},"epss":{"percentage":0.00583,"percentile":0.45567}},{"ghsa_id":"GHSA-qpxp-75px-xjcp","cve_id":"CVE-2026-33123","url":"https://api.github.com/advisories/GHSA-qpxp-75px-xjcp","html_url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-qpxp-75px-xjcp","summary":"pypdf has inefficient decoding of array-based streams","description":"### Impact\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to long runtimes and/or large memory usage. This requires accessing an array-based stream with lots of entries.\n\n### Patches\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.9.1](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.9.1).\n\n### Workarounds\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3686](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3686).","type":"reviewed","severity":"medium","repository_advisory_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/py-pdf/pypdf/security-advisories/GHSA-qpxp-75px-xjcp","source_code_location":"https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf","identifiers":[{"value":"GHSA-qpxp-75px-xjcp","type":"GHSA"},{"value":"CVE-2026-33123","type":"CVE"}],"references":["https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/security/advisories/GHSA-qpxp-75px-xjcp","https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3686","https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.9.1","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-33123","https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-qpxp-75px-xjcp"],"published_at":"2026-03-18T16:17:31Z","updated_at":"2026-03-20T21:27:32Z","github_reviewed_at":"2026-03-18T16:17:31Z","nvd_published_at":"2026-03-20T10:16:18Z","withdrawn_at":null,"vulnerabilities":[{"package":{"ecosystem":"pip","name":"pypdf"},"vulnerable_version_range":"< 6.9.1","first_patched_version":"6.9.1","vulnerable_functions":[]}],"cvss_severities":{"cvss_v3":{"vector_string":null,"score":0.0},"cvss_v4":{"vector_string":"CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N","score":5.1}},"cwes":[{"cwe_id":"CWE-400","name":"Uncontrolled Resource Consumption"},{"cwe_id":"CWE-407","name":"Inefficient Algorithmic Complexity"}],"credits":[{"user":{"login":"kule500","id":251544121,"node_id":"U_kgDODv5COQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/251544121?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kule500","html_url":"https://github.com/kule500","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kule500/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kule500/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kule500/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kule500/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kule500/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kule500/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kule500/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kule500/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kule500/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"type":"reporter"},{"user":{"login":"stefan6419846","id":96178532,"node_id":"U_kgDOBbuRZA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96178532?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefan6419846","html_url":"https://github.com/stefan6419846","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefan6419846/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefan6419846/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefan6419846/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefan6419846/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefan6419846/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefan6419846/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefan6419846/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefan6419846/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefan6419846/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"type":"analyst"}],"cvss":{"vector_string":null,"score":null},"epss":{"percentage":0.00374,"percentile":0.28572}},{"ghsa_id":"GHSA-hqmh-ppp3-xvm7","cve_id":"CVE-2026-31826","url":"https://api.github.com/advisories/GHSA-hqmh-ppp3-xvm7","html_url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-hqmh-ppp3-xvm7","summary":"pypdf: manipulated stream length values can exhaust RAM","description":"### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to large memory usage. This requires parsing a content stream with a rather large `/Length` value, regardless of the actual data length inside the stream.\n\n### Patches\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.8.0](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.8.0).\n\n### Workarounds\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3675](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3675).\n\nAs far as we are aware, this mostly affects reading from buffers of unknown size, as returned by `open(\"file.pdf\", mode=\"rb\")` for example. Passing a file path or a `BytesIO` buffer to *pypdf* instead does not seem to trigger the vulnerability.","type":"reviewed","severity":"medium","repository_advisory_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/py-pdf/pypdf/security-advisories/GHSA-hqmh-ppp3-xvm7","source_code_location":"https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf","identifiers":[{"value":"GHSA-hqmh-ppp3-xvm7","type":"GHSA"},{"value":"CVE-2026-31826","type":"CVE"}],"references":["https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/security/advisories/GHSA-hqmh-ppp3-xvm7","https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3675","https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/commit/3c550b3196adeba1506a26e57c09c09fac75e9aa","https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.8.0","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-31826","https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-hqmh-ppp3-xvm7"],"published_at":"2026-03-11T00:14:02Z","updated_at":"2026-03-11T05:46:58Z","github_reviewed_at":"2026-03-11T00:14:02Z","nvd_published_at":"2026-03-10T22:16:20Z","withdrawn_at":null,"vulnerabilities":[{"package":{"ecosystem":"pip","name":"pypdf"},"vulnerable_version_range":"< 6.8.0","first_patched_version":"6.8.0","vulnerable_functions":[]}],"cvss_severities":{"cvss_v3":{"vector_string":null,"score":0.0},"cvss_v4":{"vector_string":"CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N","score":6.8}},"cwes":[{"cwe_id":"CWE-770","name":"Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling"}],"credits":[{"user":{"login":"iconnnjka","id":87379642,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3Mzc5NjQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/87379642?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/iconnnjka","html_url":"https://github.com/iconnnjka","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/