888","url":"https://api.github.com/advisories/GHSA-x7hp-r3qg-r3cj","html_url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-x7hp-r3qg-r3cj","summary":"pypdf: Manipulated FlateDecode XFA streams can exhaust RAM","description":"### Impact\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to the RAM being exhausted. This requires accessing the `xfa` property of a reader or writer and the corresponding stream being compressed using `/FlateDecode`.\n\n### Patches\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.7.3](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.7.3).\n\n### Workarounds\nIf projects cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#3658](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3658).","type":"reviewed","severity":"medium","repository_advisory_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/py-pdf/pypdf/security-advisories/GHSA-x7hp-r3qg-r3cj","source_code_location":"https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf","identifiers":[{"value":"GHSA-x7hp-r3qg-r3cj","type":"GHSA"},{"value":"CVE-2026-27888","type":"CVE"}],"references":["https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/security/advisories/GHSA-x7hp-r3qg-r3cj","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-27888","https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/3658","https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/commit/7a4c8246ed48d9d328fb596942271da47b6d109c","https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.7.3","https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-x7hp-r3qg-r3cj"],"published_at":"2026-02-26T19:55:33Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T19:55:35Z","github_reviewed_at":"2026-02-26T19:55:33Z","nvd_published_at":"2026-02-26T01:16:25Z","withdrawn_at":null,"vulnerabilities":[{"package":{"ecosystem":"pip","name":"pypdf"},"vulnerable_version_range":"< 6.7.3","first_patched_version":"6.7.3","vulnerable_functions":[]}],"cvss_severities":{"cvss_v3":{"vector_string":null,"score":0.0},"cvss_v4":{"vector_string":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N/E:U","score":6.6}},"cwes":[{"cwe_id":"CWE-400","name":"Uncontrolled Resource Consumption"}],"credits":[{"user":{"login